Subject: Principal Unit Funding for Charter Schools - Title 14 Chapter 13 S=
ection 1307

Jennifer and Brook,

I was researching information on how Principal Units were funded as NCS has=
 four buildings but yet only earns one Principal Unit.  The excerpt below o=
ut of Title 14 Chapter 13 Section 1307 indicates that in order to qualify f=
or more than one Principal funded unit, one of two criteria must be met:

  1.  Employ 1 full-time principal for each administrative unit in a school=
 building OR
  2.  Combination of school buildings having 15 or more Division I state un=
its of pupils

NCS has four buildings under its span of responsibility as approved by all =
the Major Modifications submitted and approved by DDOE each earning more th=
an 15 DIV I units per building:

Primary School - 890590
Intermediate School - 890589
Junior High School - 890591
Senior High School - 890588

Please review this request and let me know what the next steps are in award=
ing this funded units per DE code.

Thank you.

Excerpt from DE Code Title 14 Chapter 13 Section 1307

(2) During the fiscal year beginning July 1, 1988, and annually thereafter,=
 a reorganized school district may employ 1 full-time principal for each ad=
ministrative unit in a school building or combination of school buildings h=
aving 15 or more Division I state units of pupils who shall be paid from st=
ate funds for 12 months in accordance with this section, and in accordance =
with the rules and regulations of the Department with the approval of the S=
tate Board of Education. Division I state units in excess of 15 in 1 school=
 building qualifying for a full-time principal shall not be counted toward =
entitlement for a principal for a combination of buildings.



